            <ArticleTitle>A YOUNG GIRL WITH FITS.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>232-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young girl presented with fits vomiting and epigastric pain. Investigations including CT-Scan brain, MRI brain, MRV brain and cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) examination were normal. Her urine was screened for porphobilinogen which was positive. She responded to intravenous dextrose and hypercaloric diet</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
